          "id": 1500164782,
          "type": null,
          "body": "If tcpdump is run with the `-U` flag, not only does it flush after every packet is written, it also flushes after the output file is initially created.\n\nI.e., it does the same thing that this change makes the extcaps in question do.\n\nI see precisely zero reason why those extcaps should not do this.\n\n> This means you can no longer do a capture to a FIFO or Named Pipe in this order:\n\n\"Doctor, it hurts when I do this!\"\n\n\"So don't do that.\"",
